<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Sugar buys 30,000T US corn/soy at tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Sugar buys 30,000T US corn/soy at tender.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Taiwan Sugar Corp on Wednesday bought a combined shipment of 18,000 tonnes U.S. corn and 12,000 U.S. soybean from Zennoh at a tender, traders said.  </p>
<p>The shipment's was fixed on a cost and freight basis, traders said.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p>		     U.S. Gulf  Pacific N.W.  Price/Futures</p>
<p> Corn    18,000  Aug 5-20   Aug 21-Sep 5   97.58 US cents/Sep</p>
<p> Soybean 12,000  Aug 5-20   Aug 21-Sep 5  196.98 US cents/Sep</p>
<p>--Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
